he AI Act, and regulation as it relates to start-ups and the innovation economy Ensuring that the regulation that is passed allows start-ups using artificial intelligence to compete with larger technology incumbents and that the access of information and talent is competitive across democratic nations This relates to all of the subcomponents of the AI Act, including transparency, and regulation, from companies that use artificial intelligence to leaders like foundation model providers','2025-09-20 15:06:28'),(123665,'Digital Markets Act','2025-09-20 15:06:29'),(123666,'Digital Services Act','2025-09-20 15:06:29'),(123667,'European Media Freedom Act','2025-09-20 15:06:29'),(123668,'ePrivacy','2025-09-20 15:06:29'),(123669,'Digital Fairness Act','2025-09-20 15:06:29'),(123670,'Audiovisual and media policies','2025-09-20 15:06:30'),(123671,'No other items to declare to this register','2025-09-20 15:06:30'),(123672,'All initiatives, policies and legislative in the fields of VAT, Customs and any other indirect taxes','2025-09-20 15:06:31'),(123673,'All Council Directives, Council Implementing Regulations and Council Implementing Decisions and Guidelines relating to VAT, Customs and any other indirect taxes, particularly but not restricted to Council Directive 2006/112/EC and related acts','2025-09-20 15:06:31'),(123674,'Common Fisheries Policy (CFP) Common Organisation of the Markets (CMO)','2025-09-20 15:06:32'),(123675,'Pelagic Advisory Council (PELAC)','2025-09-20 15:06:32'),(123676,'Long Distance Advisory Council (LDAC)','2025-09-20 15:06:32'),(123677,'North Western Waters Advisory Council (NWWAC)','2025-09-20 15:06:32'),(123678,'Markets Advisory Council (MAC)','2025-09-20 15:06:32'),(123679,'EU Directives currently of major importance: Marine Strategy Framework Single Use Plastics Working Time EU Green Deal (Climate Adaptation) Marine Spatial Planning  This list is not definitive and other EU Directives and legislation may assume greater importance in response to un