stech společné zahraniční a bezpečnostní politiky a vnitřního trhu v těch otázkách, kde jsou zahrnuty i zájmy našich členů Příkladem je Green Deal, nařízení REACH, problematika tranzitních licencí, Evropský obranný fond','2025-09-20 15:12:34'),(125645,'The relevant policy and regulatory areas cover a broad spectrum, including the Energy Union Strategy and the Internal Energy Market, the EU Emissions Trading System (ETS), External Energy Policy, and the 2030 Climate and Energy Framework Further key initiatives comprise the EU Infrastructure Package, the Regulation on Energy Market Integrity and Transparency (REMIT), the Markets in Financial Instruments Directive (MiFID), and the European Market Infrastructure Regulation (EMIR) Important environmental and product standards are addressed through the EcoDesign and Energy Labelling Framework, broader Environmental Policy measures, and the Clean Air Package The Digital Agenda for Europe underpins efforts towards digitalization, while dedicated legislation regulates Renewable Energy Sources, Energy Efficiency, Biofuels, and the Fuel Quality Directive Strategic initiatives also include the Heating and Cooling Strategy, policies on Energy Storage Development, and measures supporting Carbon Capture and Storage (CCS)','2025-09-20 15:12:35'),(125646,'In the area of energy markets, focus is given to the Electricity and Gas Market Design, including implementation through ACER, CEER, ENTSO-G, and ENTSO-E Network Codes Substantial financial support is provided via various EU Funding Mechanisms such as the European Structural and Investment Funds (ESIF), the Connecting Europe Facility (CEF), Projects of Common Interest (PCI), Horizon 2020, the EU Energy Programme for Recovery, the NER 300 programme, and the European Fund for Strategic Investments (EFSI) Additionally, the European Green Deal and its associated initiatives, the comprehensive Fit for 55 legislative package targeting the 2030 climate objectives, the Regulation on fluorinated greenhouse gases (F-Gas Regulation), and the Next Generation EU recovery instrument represent critical pillars for achieving Europe’s long-term energy, climate, and sustainability goals','2025-09-20 15:12:35'),(125647,'Main activities:','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125648,'European policy affecting the competitiveness of manufacturing','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125649,'Technical and regulatory affairs, on standards, certification and harmonisation:','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125650,'-	Machinery Directive and regulation','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125651,'-	Energy using Products EuP','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125652,'-       Ecodesign','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125653,'-	Labelling (water and energy using products)','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125654,'-	REACH/RoHS','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125655,'-       Clean industrial deal','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125656,'-       Chemical industry package','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125657,'-	Electric motors in vacuum cleaners','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125658,'-	European machinery certification systems eg PM10','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125659,'-	Artificial Intelligence, Data and Cyber-Security','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125660,'-	Outdoor Noise','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125661,'-	Standardisation Strategy','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125662,'Civil Society dialogue on Trade topics, on regulatory convergence to reduce non-tariff barriers:','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125663,'-	Bilateral trade agreements','2025-09-20 15:12:36'),(125664,'- Annual resolutions of the EP on EIB activities','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125665,'- European Fund for Strategic Investments','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125666,'- European External Investment Plan (EFSD)','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125667,'- NDICI','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125668,'- Global Gateway','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125669,'- Tax issues and anti-money laundering policies','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125670,'- European Green Deal & the Sustainable Europe Investment Plan','2025-09-20 15:12:37'),(125671,'- Recovery and Resilience Facility','2