 organization supports the development of the Romanian National Registry of Pediatric Oncology and Hematology (RNOHP), via the strategic partnership undertaken with the Romanian Society of Pediatric Oncology-Hematology RNOHP is an essential resource to survival chances improvement for the children with cancer in Romania, being the main objective source of information on their needs and for the planning of Pediatric Oncology (PO) services development in our country For the first time, Romanian health officials eg the Ministry of Health became aware of the incidence and survival rate for child cancer at national level','2025-09-20 15:16:26'),(126734,'In October 2018, the National Registry of Pediatric Oncology and Hematology (RNOHP) was accepted for affiliation by the European Network of Cancer Registries (wwwencreu) an indication that RCCR meets the quality criteria imposed by ENCR for cancer registries, thus allowing Romania to participate with actual data in international statistics on childhood cancer','2025-09-20 15:16:26'),(126735,'Daruieste Aripi experts experts have produced two survival studies (in 2019 and in 2024) using data from the Registry (RNOHP) Both studies are validated by experts from the European Network of Cancer Registries The results of the 2024 study, presented in the Romanian Parliament, highlight a significant difference in survival rates between children in rural areas and those in urban areas (67% in rural areas vs 75% in urban areas), as well as between different regions of the country: Bucharest/Ilfov (76%) versus North East/South East (68%)','2025-09-20 15:16:26'),(126736,'Further details about the results of the 2024 survival study can be consulted on the Daruieste Aripi website at https://wwwdaruiestearipiro/en/survival-of-children-with-cancer-diagnosed-between-2014-2017/','2025-09-20 15:16:26'),(126737,'Wir beobachten derzeit intensiv ua die Verhandlungen zur Richtlinie mit neuen Vorschriften für Verträge zwischen Unternehmen und Verb