cts (IDEP), an apolitical organization recognized at the national, regional, and European levels for its high-impact initiatives discussed with key stakeholders in European and regional public policy during high-level debates In securing support from European authorities for IDEP’s projects, we have focused on several key initiatives These include “Europe in the Citizen’s Home, Community, and Small Business” (ECIPES https://bitly/3kTAk93 – https://bitly/MEP_WQ_ECIPES), which led to the introduction of its most important element —the “Rabla Electrocasnice” program “Market Access” (the EU–Republic of Moldova Highway http://bitly/ 3AMDBiS a question submitted to the European Parliament https://wwweuroparleuropaeu/doceo/ document/E-8-2019-002017_ENhtml, prompting stakeholders to endorse the highway https://midrgovmd/ noutati/prima-etapa-in-construirea-autostrazii-iasi-ungheni-chisinau-odesa) and a recreational initiative, “DiscoverEU Iași–Chișinău” ( http://bitly/3nVTnQT), along with related questions addressed by MEPs to the European Commission (http://bitly/DiscoverEUIasiChisinauOdesa)','2025-09-20 15:22:01'),(128244,'With the aim of bringing the communities on both banks of the Prut River closer together and establishing Moldovan–Romanian project partnerships, IDEP initiated 15 discussion forums that brought together over 1,800 leaders under the theme “Boosting the Absorption of European Funds by Moldova” (details here: http://bitly/IDEP-delegatii – agendas, photos, and press articles) As a result, numerous sectoral and inter-institutional partnerships were established between counterparts on both banks of the Prut','2025-09-20 15:22:01'),(128245,'Additionally, we wish to inform you that on June 4, 2025, we organized a debate in the European Parliament Following this debate, we approved together with the participants the text of a Call to Action, which was sent to the authorities of Romania, Moldova, and Ukraine, and also to the leadership of the European Commission 